## 5. Base path confirmation

- The `/api` prefix comes from the **directory layout**, not a property: the file lives at `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. OfficeFloor/WoOF maps `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/<path>.<HTTP-METHOD>.yml` to `<HTTP-METHOD> /<path>`, so this file = **`POST /api/owners`**. There is no top-level `officefloor/*.yml` (e.g. objects.yml/teams.yml) overriding paths, and no additional base-path property.
- There IS a servlet context path in **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/application.properties`**:
  ```
  server.port=9966
  server.servlet.context-path=/petclinic/
  ```
  So the fully-qualified URL at runtime is `POST http://localhost:9966/petclinic/api/owners`, while the logical REST endpoint (the part defined by the pipeline path) is `POST /api/owners`. The same `context-path=/petclinic/` is set in the test properties.

Also relevant: **`petclinic.security.enable=false`** in `application.properties` (security is disabled by default, which affects whether the `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` authorize check is enforced at runtime).
